2026-07-27T16:20:52,local,Full context (original),Gemini (vision),answered,i am unable to add a property,"Hi there! I see exactly what is holding you up in your screenshot. 

It looks like the system is blocking you from moving to the next step because of two missing mandatory fields on the **Basic Information** page. 

### How to resolve this:

1. **Select a Category**: Click the **Select Category** dropdown and choose your property category (such as **Residential Lettings** or **Commercial Lettings**).
2. **Add a Reference Number**: You can either type your own unique reference into the **Reference number** box, or simply click the blue **Generate Reference number** link to have the system create one for you.
3. Click the green **NEXT** button to proceed to the next step.

Give that a try and let me know if it lets you move forward! Once you get past this screen, would you like me to walk you through what to expect on the upcoming steps?",,
2026-07-27T16:26:01,local,Full context (original),Gemini,answered,unable to get my video uploaded to the property,"Hi there! I can certainly help you get that video sorted for your property listing. 

In our system, you actually don't upload raw video files (like an .mp4) directly from your computer. Instead, the system is designed to host videos via links. 

Here is how you can add your video:

### How to Add Your Video Link
1. Navigate to your property record and go to **Page 2 – Property Details** (or the media edit section of an existing property).
2. Scroll down to the **Additional Media** section.
3. Paste your video link into the designated field. The system currently supports:
   * **YouTube Video URL**
   * **TikTok Video Widget URL**

To help me get this working for you, are you trying to upload a raw video file from your computer, or are you having trouble getting a YouTube or TikTok link to save?",,
2026-07-27T16:26:42,local,Full context (original),Gemini,answered,It is neither it is a 360 tour link,"Ah, got it! My apologies for the mix-up. 

A **360° Virtual Tour** is absolutely supported in the system, and it has its own dedicated spot right next to the video links.

Here is where you can add it:

### How to Add Your 360° Virtual Tour
1. Go to **Page 2 – Property Details** of your property record.
2. Scroll down to the **Additional Media** section (just below where you upload standard images).
3. Look for the **360° Virtual Tour URLs** field.
4. Paste your virtual tour link directly into that field and click **Next** or **Submit** to save.

Are you currently editing an existing property, or are you adding a brand new one from scratch? I can guide you through the exact steps to get to that screen if you'd like!",,
2026-07-27T16:27:15,local,Full context (original),Gemini,answered,It is an existing property,"Since you are updating an existing property, you will just need to locate the property in your system first to edit it. 

Here is how you can update it:

### 1. Locate Your Property
1. Navigate to your property list (you can find your properties listed under **All Properties**).
2. Search for and select the existing property you want to update.
3. Open the edit form for that property.

### 2. Add the 360° Tour Link
1. Go to **Page 2 – Property Details** of the edit wizard.
2. Scroll down to the **Additional Media** section (located right below the image upload area).
3. Paste your link into the **360° Virtual Tour URLs** field.
4. Proceed through the remaining pages and click **Submit** on the final page to save your changes and update the portals.

*(Note: While our guides don't show the exact button-by-button path for opening the edit screen on an existing property, it is typically accessed directly from your main property list.)*

Give that a try! Let me know if you run into any trouble finding the property or saving the link.",,
